Extension API: the Info screen's history scale and turn messages on the wire ("INFS").

STATUS: NOT APPLIED. Written by work order 175 D, 26 September 2026, and
parked for Data's go/no-go (doc/briefs/175-parked-for-data.md). What was
shown, and only this: the patch applies to src/ext/ext_api.cpp at orion2re
orionlayer-local cc542e02 (`patch -p1 --dry-run`), and the patched file
compiles with the engine's own flags from
out/build/Linux/linux-debug/build.ninja (g++ -std=gnu++20 -fsyntax-only,
the cmake_pch.hxx include, the ORION2RE_EXT define) — with a control: the
same file with one member name misspelt is refused. It has not run.

To apply, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_info_screen_state.patch

then rebuild, and add the INFS marker to tools/version_check.py in the
commit that records the apply (the pattern of open fixes 30 and 31).

WHAT IT IS FOR

    INFO::Info_Screen_ (info.cpp:510-642) draws two pages from state
    SerializeState never sends:

      - the HISTORY GRAPH (info.cpp:1222-1329): the four history rings are
        in s_player and on the wire, but they are stored DIVIDED by
        MOX::_bill_savegame[2..5] (bill.cpp:445-535), and past 350 turns
        they start at _bill_savegame[1] (Get_History_Params_,
        bill.cpp:547-556). Without those six numbers the curves of more
        than one metric cannot be added and the y axis cannot be labelled.
      - the TURN SUMMARY (info.cpp:2011-2112): MSG_::_msgs is not in the
        snapshot at all, and each line is MSG_::sprintf_msg_ over formats
        in RSTRING<lang>.LBX and names from half a dozen tables.

    RECONSTRUCTION WAS TRIED FIRST (decision 25): the rings, the stardate
    and the players are on the wire; the divisors are not derivable (they
    only ever grow, turn by turn, from values no longer in any array), and
    the messages are nowhere on the wire.

THE BLOCK, appended after OFFS's position, only while SCREEN_INFO is up:

    "INFS"
    int16  _bill_savegame[0..5]
    int16  N                       the player's messages
    N x (int16 length, length bytes)   each rendered by sprintf_msg_

One file, src/ext/ext_api.cpp. Nothing above the block moves.

--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -396,6 +396,47 @@
             Write8(buf, (uint8_t)(MOX::_fltscrn_big_icon[i].selected != 0));
         }
     }
+
+    // 5. The Info screen's two inputs SerializeState never sent: "INFS",
+    //    written ONLY while SCREEN_INFO is up, and LAST, so nothing above
+    //    it moves and a client that stops earlier is unaffected. It can
+    //    never meet OFFS or FLTS (other screens). OrionLayer, open fix 32.
+    //
+    //    - MOX::_bill_savegame[6] (mox.cpp:778): [1] is where the history
+    //      rings start once a game is past 350 turns (Get_History_Params_,
+    //      bill.cpp:547-556) and [2..5] are the divisors the four rings
+    //      were scaled by (bill.cpp:445-535). The rings themselves are in
+    //      s_player, on the wire already; without these six numbers the
+    //      History Graph cannot be drawn or labelled (info.cpp:1222-1329).
+    //    - the Turn Summary's messages, RENDERED exactly as the screen
+    //      renders them (MSG_::sprintf_msg_, info.cpp:1971), in the
+    //      player's slice of MSG_::_msgs (msg.cpp:86-114). The formats
+    //      live in RSTRING<lang>.LBX and the names in half a dozen tables,
+    //      so sending the finished strings is the one form a client can
+    //      use without re-implementing sprintf_msg_. Raw bytes, the game's
+    //      8-bit text with its FMTPARA codes; int16 length first.
+    if (current_screen == SCREEN_INFO) {
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'I');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'N');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'F');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'S');
+        for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
+            Write16(buf, MOX::_bill_savegame[i]);
+        }
+        int16_t first = MSG_::First_Msg_For_Player_(MOX::_PLAYER_NUM);
+        int16_t n = MSG_::N_Msgs_For_Player_(MOX::_PLAYER_NUM);
+        if (first < 0 || first >= MAX_MESSAGES || n < 0) n = 0;
+        if (first + n > MAX_MESSAGES) n = (int16_t)(MAX_MESSAGES - first);
+        Write16(buf, n);
+        char text[256];
+        for (int16_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+            MSG_::sprintf_msg_(text, sizeof(text), &MSG_::_msgs[first + i]);
+            size_t len = strnlen(text, sizeof(text));
+            Write16(buf, (int16_t)len);
+            buf.insert(buf.end(), (const uint8_t*)text,
+                       (const uint8_t*)text + len);
+        }
+    }
 }
 
